  "prompt": "# Adversarial review \u2014 GPS through the sink + runtime debug mirror (#411)\n\nAdversarial embedded C++ review. Offband MeshCore firmware (nRF52 + ESP32). This makes the\nserial-capture sink the single runtime debug path and routes GPS through it. Changes:\n\n1. `MeshLog`: adds a `g_meshLogMirror` flag (default true) + `meshLogSetMirror`. `mesh_log_line`\n   now ALSO writes the formatted line to `Serial` (outside the lock) when `g_meshLogMirror`, in\n   addition to the ring append. Both are gated by `g_meshLogEnabled` + level.\n2. `MeshCore.h`: `MESH_DEBUG_PRINTLN` is now ALWAYS `if (g_meshLogEnabled) mesh_log_line(...)` \u2014\n   the old compile-time `#if MESH_DEBUG` `Serial.printf` branch is RETIRED. `MESH_DEBUG_PRINT`\n   (fragments) stays compile-gated.\n3. `BaseSerialInterface::isConsoleSharedWithProtocol()` (default false) + `ArduinoSerialInterface`\n   override (`_serial == &Serial`). `companion_radio/main.cpp` sets `meshLogSetMirror(!shared)`\n   after `startInterface` on every platform branch.\n4. `EnvironmentSensorManager` `[GPS]` + `MicroNMEALocationProvider` `[GPSPARSE]` raw `Serial.print`\n   \u2192 `mesh_log_line(MLOG_DEBUG, ...)`.\n\nIntent: client sets `caplog start [level]` \u2192 debug (incl GPS) is captured AND mirrored to live\nserial where the console is free (repeater/observer/BLE-companion), but NOT on a USB-serial\ncompanion (mirror off there, so nothing raw hits the framed protocol line).\n\nReview concretely (cite file:line, rank severity):\n1. The mirror in `mesh_log_line`: `Serial.write` outside the critical section \u2014 reentrancy/ordering\n   vs concurrent producers (main loop + BLE task both logging)? Could interleaved `Serial.write`s\n   from two tasks corrupt each other on the console? Is that acceptable vs the protocol-line case?\n2. `isConsoleSharedWithProtocol` correctness: `_serial == &Serial` \u2014 right for USB companion (true)\n   and UART-bridge/BLE (false)? Any platform where `&Serial` comparison is wrong? Default false safe?\n3. Macro change: any regression from removing the `#if MESH_DEBUG` serial branch? Double-print\n   anywhere now? Hot-path cost when disabled (args unevaluated)? Any build that relied on the old\n   compile-time serial output?\n4. GPS routing: `mesh_log_line(MLOG_DEBUG, \"[GPS] %s\\n\", _gps_b)` \u2014 format-string safety (is\n   `_gps_b` ever attacker/format-bearing?), the `[GPSPARSE]` printf arg types/casts.\n5. Anything missed \u2014 a build where `Serial` isn't valid, mirror default causing spam, etc.\n\nTerse. If sound, say so.\n\n=== C:\\Users\\stryc\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\claude\\C--Dev-meshcore-firmware\\ce5045af-5978-4a55-8b3c-9ce0975d4fe7\\scratchpad\\411-diff.txt ===\ndiff --git a/examples/companion_radio/main.cpp b/examples/companion_radio/main.cpp\nindex f0a5b2a9..c160abe2 100644\n--- a/examples/companion_radio/main.cpp\n+++ b/examples/companion_radio/main.cpp\n@@ -259,6 +259,10 @@ void setup() {\n   serial_interface.begin(Serial);\n #endif\n   the_mesh.startInterface(serial_interface);\n+  // #411: mirror captured serial-log lines to the live console EXCEPT where the\n+  // framed protocol runs on Serial itself (USB-serial companion) -- there it stays\n+  // capture-only so nothing raw corrupts the protocol line.\n+  meshLogSetMirror(!serial_interface.isConsoleSharedWithProtocol());\n #elif defined(RP2040_PLATFORM)\n   LittleFS.begin();\n   store.begin();\n@@ -285,6 +289,10 @@ void setup() {\n     serial_interface.begin(Serial);\n   #endif\n     the_mesh.startInterface(serial_interface);\n+  // #411: mirror captured serial-log lines to the live console EXCEPT where the\n+  // framed protocol runs on Serial itself (USB-serial companion) -- there it stays\n+  // capture-only so nothing raw corrupts the protocol line.\n+  meshLogSetMirror(!serial_interface.isConsoleSharedWithProtocol());\n #elif defined(ESP32)\n   CW_PHASE(\"ESP32:before SPIFFS.begin\");\n   SPIFFS.begin(true);\n@@ -331,6 +339,10 @@ void setup() {\n   CW_PHASE(\"ESP